        "original_id": "6162bc6e-8004-56e2-a310-6d4d2fe23393",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: NBA 2K16, NBA 2K17, Come, Zanaka\n- People: Tony Parker, Dennis Schröder, Marc Gasol, Pau Gasol, Jain\n- Organizations: San Antonio Spurs, Atlanta Hawks, Memphis Grizzlies, Chicago Bulls\n- Roles: cover athletes, point guard\n- Concepts: NBA 2K franchise\n\nFacts:\n- NBA 2K16 has regional cover athletes including Tony Parker for the French version, Dennis Schröder for the German version, and Marc and Pau Gasol for the Spanish version.\n- Tony Parker was with the San Antonio Spurs when he was featured as the French cover athlete for NBA 2K16.\n- Dennis Schröder was with the Atlanta Hawks when he was featured as the German cover athlete for NBA 2K16.\n- Marc Gasol was with the Memphis Grizzlies and Pau Gasol was with the Chicago Bulls when they were featured as the Spanish cover athletes for NBA 2K16.\n- NBA 2K17 is the 18th installment in the NBA 2K franchise and succeeds NBA 2K16.\n- The song Come is by Jain from the album Zanaka and was featured in NBA 2K17.\n- Dennis Schröder plays the point guard position.",
